# Shell scripts must be committed with LF endings, always.
#
# stream-server/setup.sh was once committed with CRLF. Every server that
# downloaded it got `set -euo pipefail\r` on line one, which bash rejects with
# "invalid option name: pipefail" — an error that names the wrong thing and
# looks like a corrupt download. Diagnosing that on a console with no
# copy/paste, during an outage, cost hours.
#
# eol=lf normalises on commit, so a checkout from Windows or an editor that
# rewrites endings can no longer put a CR into anything meant to be executed.
*.sh text eol=lf
